# Everything not needed to build or run the app.
#
# The rule is deny-by-default where it is cheap to be, because the two things
# that must never reach a build context are secrets and the author's own
# content. `.env.local` holds the session secret and the database URL; copying
# it into an image layer is a credential leak that survives every later
# deletion, since layers are additive.

# Secrets and local configuration.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The author's content and media. Mounted as volumes at run time, never baked
# into an image — the image is the application, and the application is the same
# whatever is published with it. `uploads/` is the host side of the compose bind
# mount and `public/uploads/` is where a local dev server writes; neither is
# source.
content/
public/uploads/
uploads/

# Dependencies and build output: reinstalled inside the build stage, where the
# platform and the lockfile are the ones that matter.
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.next/
out/
dist/

# Version control and editors.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Tests, fixtures and their reports. Not shipped, and their fixtures are large.
tests/
playwright-report/
test-results/
coverage/

# Documentation and tooling that has no bearing on the image.
*.md
!README.md
LICENSE
.editorconfig
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml

# Logs and OS noise.
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
